{"diagnosis": "Fetch made no progress with max_addr=0x00000000 vs expected advancing PC over 256 NOP words, yielding tohost FAIL 0xdead and TRAP: no progress. Root cause in excerpt at picorv32.v:392 is reset of mem_la_firstword_reg to 0 instead of 1, so the first post-reset fetch is treated as a continuation word and dropped, stalling the core. Trace wins over empty CONE_SLICE; VERDICT FAIL 0xdead confirms the stall.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -390,9 +390,9 @@
 always @(posedge clk) begin
 	if (!resetn) begin
-		mem_la_firstword_reg <= 0;
+		mem_la_firstword_reg <= 1;
 		last_mem_valid <= 0;
 	end else begin
 		if (!last_mem_valid)
 			mem_la_firstword_reg <= mem_la_firstword;
 		last_mem_valid <= mem_valid && !mem_ready;
 	end
 end
", "expected": "tohost PASS (not FAIL 0xdead), no TRAP: no progress, max_addr progress >0x00000000 over 256 NOPs"}

